	(text "1. RELAY ENABLE  SAFE_EN = SAFE_GPIO (IO3) AND watchdog OK"(exclude_from_sim no)(at 25.40 25.40 0)(effects(font(size 2.0 2.0))(justify left top))(uuid "9777a9ec-54bd-4c3c-8aad-3cb8fbbcab41"))
	(text "2. USB + 5V SURGE PROTECTION"(exclude_from_sim no)(at 25.40 106.68 0)(effects(font(size 2.0 2.0))(justify left top))(uuid "b8b4ba93-f192-4a78-b2da-219fe18db08f"))
	(text "3. ESD ON EXTERNAL CABLES  (put each diode close to its connector on the PCB)"(exclude_from_sim no)(at 25.40 160.02 0)(effects(font(size 2.0 2.0))(justify left top))(uuid "d2aebb19-2169-4c95-b5b2-e4c8e6bf5e5d"))
	(text "4. REFRIGERANT LEAK SENSOR  (ADS1115 #3 at 0x4B)"(exclude_from_sim no)(at 203.20 25.40 0)(effects(font(size 2.0 2.0))(justify left top))(uuid "540041b7-4574-437c-9a66-bc0ffa91fd5c"))
	(text "HOW IT WORKS\n- SAFE_EN goes over the ribbon (pin 12) to the power board and switches the relay-coil supply.\n  It is only HIGH when firmware drives IO3 high AND the TPS3823 watchdog is not in reset.\n  R53 holds IO3 low while the ESP32 boots, so relays can never click on at power-up.\n- The watchdog cuts the relays even if the WDT_EN jumper is removed (jumper only controls ESP32 reset).\n- ESTOP_OK / HP_OK come back on ribbon pins 19/20 into MCP23017 GPB6 / GPB7.\n- Leak sensor: any 5V sensor with 0-5V analog output (e.g. a refrigerant/halocarbon gas sensor).\n  R54/R55 scale 5V down to 3.2V for the ADS1115. Firmware: on leak -> stop, run COND_FAN, alarm.\n- Load cell lines have no extra TVS (NAU7802 has its own ESD protection and TVS leakage would hurt accuracy)."(exclude_from_sim no)(at 203.20 106.68 0)(effects(font(size 1.27 1.27))(justify left top))(uuid "c74bc7a9-9327-4df3-aa47-70f5984aa88b"))
	(global_label "P4_ADC"(shape passive)(at 297.18 66.04 180)(fields_autoplaced yes)(effects(font(size 1.27 1.27))(justify right))(uuid "6e54ea9a-4c28-42e9-b0b5-6ff3507c6856")(property "Intersheetrefs" "${INTERSHEET_REFS}"(at 297.18 66.04 0)(effects(font(size 1.27 1.27))(hide yes))))
